LICENSE — ready to add to the repo (final text + 2-minute steps)
Prepared 2026-10-24. The repo is public with no LICENSE file (verified live
2026-10-24: root contains extension/, store-assets/, versions/, .gitignore,
DATA_USAGE.md, MAINTENANCE_CHECKLIST.md, PRIVACY.md, README.md,
SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md, TERMS.md, manifest.json — no LICENSE).
No license already means all rights reserved; writing it down removes the
"I thought it was open source" defence and makes any takedown faster.
Costs nothing, changes no code, does not affect the store review in progress.
1. File content — create LICENSE at the repo root with exactly this text
Copyright (c) 2026 Annie Tan. All rights reserved.

This repository is public so the code can be viewed, discussed, and
referenced for portfolio and educational purposes.

No license is granted to copy, modify, distribute, publish, or create
derivative works from this code, in whole or in part — including as part
of another browser extension or product — without the prior written
permission of the copyright holder.

Viewing this repository and forking it within GitHub (as permitted by
GitHub's Terms of Service) do not grant any right to use the code
outside of GitHub.
One check before saving: the copyright line says "Annie Tan" (taken from the
store account name annietan9011). Change it if you prefer a different name.
2. Optional README addition — paste under a ## License heading
## License

Copyright © 2026 Annie Tan. All rights reserved. This project is
source-visible, not open source: the code is public for viewing and
discussion, and may not be copied, modified, or redistributed without
permission. See [LICENSE](LICENSE).
3. Steps — GitHub web UI, ~2 minutes, no git, no tokens
Open https://github.com/atan141/academic-evidence-highlighter
Click Add file → Create new file
Name the file LICENSE (all caps, no extension)
Paste the text from section 1
Commit changes... → commit directly to main
(Optional) open README.md → pencil icon → add the section from part 2 →
   commit. The README currently has a "Policy Documents" section listing
   PRIVACY.md / TERMS.md / DATA_USAGE.md — the License section fits right
   after it.
